    "body": "## Problem\n\nA prepare pass already materializes a bounded public-surface candidate window, then can issue the same pending-work SQL again at its tail. Reuse that actual window when the final seed list exactly matches the queried list and admission stays within the original budget.\n\n## Change and resulting behavior\n\n- Keep the window local to one prepare call. Preserve the original SQL fallback when seeds expand, the window is missing, or admission bounds do not match.\n- Preserve the existing unconditional prepared-build epoch check, transactional fences, candidate ordering, budgets, and cursor behavior.\n- Add six focused Rust controls covering SQL equivalence, exact-basis requirements, replacement/removal/reopen, promotion behavior, expanded-seed fallback, and external-write epoch rejection.\n- Add one fixed-head controls workflow that also runs the three existing dependency-window controls and the existing stale-prepared-build test.\n- Follow #170: retain its reviewed snapshot batching product and current validation integration. The additional production change is confined to reconcile.rs. #170 remains available with its own actual CI evidence.\n\n## Review and execution\n\nThe actual P → R → G objects were independently reviewed before first publication:\n\n- Product: `a402e88d460179afb12e3e2dc066d62cf168c690`\n- Review: `f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175`\n- Fixed head: `275e8799d4947d297329073eaa3ca675d3fd0777`\n- Source inventory: 1,089 product inputs, 41 historical deltas, 139 validation inputs.\n- [Independent source review](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/blob/f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175/artifacts/checkpoints/p8-surface-window-controls-20261009/independent-source-review.json)\n- [Execution plan](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/blob/f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175/artifacts/checkpoints/p8-surface-window-controls-20261009/original-execution-plan.json)\n\nNative Rust 1.95 rustfmt preparation completed on the fixed candidate. The first controls run and this PR's unchanged original CI must now execute on the published head; earlier PR results are not substituted for them. The v15 verifier changes contain only the four reviewed identity constants. Original CI, six frozen historical proof files, task definitions, and acceptance criteria are unchanged.\n\n## Current acceptance boundary\n\nNo measured speedup or additional TODO completion is claimed. This removes one eligible final query; prefix rescans across separate prepare calls remain. The original a23 formal N150 study continues unchanged and this engineering follow-up adds no prerequisite to its ten-task closure.\n\nCurrent original ledger: **192 total / 163 done / 29 remaining; 0 newly closed in this round**.\n",
